type-body-3">Author: </p><p class="flex-none max-w-30 relative whitespace-pre-wrap break-words type-body-3 text-white-a50">Inês Marques</p></div></div></div></section><section class="items-center bg-white-token-2 flex flex-none flex-col gap-20 h-min justify-center relative w-full z-1 px-6 py-20 m:pb-30 l:pr-32.75 l:pl-62"><section id="detail" class="items-center flex flex-none flex-col gap-3 h-208.5 justify-center absolute w-full top-0 left-[calc(50%_-_100%_/_2)]"><div class="items-center flex flex-1 shrink-0 basis-0 h-px justify-center relative w-full"><div class="bg-white-token-2 flex-none h-full relative w-full" style="transform:none"></div></div></section><div class="bg-black-a16 flex-none h-px max-w-360 overflow-clip relative w-full"></div><div class="items-start flex flex-none flex-col gap-7.5 h-min justify-center max-w-360 overflow-clip relative w-full m:flex-row m:gap-47.5" style="opacity:0"><div class="items-center flex flex-none gap-2.5 h-min justify-start max-w-10 relative w-full m:flex-1 m:shrink-0 m:basis-0 m:w-px"><p class="flex-1 shrink-0 basis-0 relative whitespace-pre-wrap w-px break-words type-body-1 text-black-token">001</p></div><div class="items-start flex flex-none flex-col gap-10 h-min justify-start overflow-clip relative w-full m:flex-1 m:shrink-0 m:basis-0 m:w-px"><div class="items-start flex flex-none gap-51.75 h-min justify-start overflow-clip relative w-full"><h2 class="flex-1 shrink-0 basis-0 relative whitespace-pre-wrap w-px break-words type-heading-4 text-black-token">Meaning</h2></div><div class="items-start flex flex-none flex-col gap-10 h-min justify-center max-w-177.5 overflow-clip relative w-full"><div class="flex flex-col justify-start shrink-0 flex-none relative whitespace-pre-wrap w-full break-words rich-text [&amp;_p]:type-body-2"><p>Before we open a colour picker, we talk about meaning. What should people feel when they see this brand? Calm, energised, reassured? The answers point us towards a temperature and a mood long before we choose a single hex code.</p><p>We also look at the category. If every competitor uses blue, a confident green or warm red can help a brand stand out on a crowded shelf or a busy feed. Standing apart is useful, but only when the colour still fits the story the brand wants to tell.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="items-center flex flex-none flex-col gap-2.5 h-min justify-center max-w-360 relative w-full m:flex-row"><div class="flex-none h-105 overflow-clip relative w-full rounded-[5px] m:flex-1 m:shrink-0 m:basis-0 m:h-130 m:w-px" style="opacity:0"><img alt="Portrait blurred by movement" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="rounded-[inherit] object-cover object-center" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="/images/blog/designing-for-motion-1.webp"/></div><div class="flex-none h-105 max-w-[unset] overflow-clip relative w-full rounded-[5px] m:flex-1 m:shrink-0 m:basis-0 m:h-130 m:max-w-87.5 m:w-px" style="opacity:0"><img alt="Orange trainers on a blue and orange set" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="rounded-[inherit] object-cover object-center" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="/images/blog/designing-for-motion-2.webp"/></div></div><div class="items-start flex flex-none flex-col gap-7.5 h-min justify-center max-w-360 overflow-clip relative w-full m:flex-row m:gap-47.5" style="opacity:0"><div class="items-center flex flex-none gap-2.5 h-min justify-start max-w-10 relative w-full m:flex-1 m:shrink-0 m:basis-0 m:w-px"><p class="flex-1 shrink-0 basis-0 relative whitespace-pre-wrap w-px break-words type-body-1 text-black-token">002</p></div><div class="items-start flex flex-none flex-col gap-10 h-min justify-start overflow-clip relative w-full m:flex-1 m:shrink-0 m:basis-0 m:w-px"><div class="items-start flex flex-none gap-51.75 h-min justify-start overflow-clip relative w-full"><h2 class="flex-1 shrink-0 basis-0 relative whitespace-pre-wrap w-px break-words type-heading-4 text-black-token">Contrast</h2></div><div class="items-start flex flex-none flex-col gap-10 h-min justify-center max-w-177.5 overflow-clip relative w-full"><div class="flex flex-col justify-start shrink-0 flex-none relative whitespace-pre-wrap w-full break-words rich-text [&amp;_p]:type-body-2"><p>A palette has to work in the real world, not just in a presentation. We check every pairing for contrast so text stays readable on screens, in print and for people with low vision. If a favourite combination fails the test, we adjust it rather than ignore the problem.<br><br>We also test colours on the materials they will live on: coated and uncoated paper, fabric, packaging and phone screens at full and low brightness. The same shade can look completely different on each, so we pick values that hold together across all of them.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="items-center flex flex-none flex-col gap-2.5 h-min justify-center max-w-360 relative w-full m:flex-row"><div class="flex-none h-105 relative w-full rounded-[5px] m:flex-1 m:shrink-0 m:basis-0 m:h-130 m:w-px" style="opacity:0"><img alt="Runner on a hillside at sunset" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="rounded-[inherit] object-cover object-center" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="/images/blog/designing-for-motion-3.webp"/></div></div><div class="items-start flex flex-none flex-col gap-7.5 h-min justify-center max-w-360 overflow-clip relative w-full m:flex-row m:gap-47.5" style="opacity:0"><div class="items-center flex flex-none gap-2.5 h-min justify-start max-w-10 relative w-full m:flex-1 m:shrink-0 m:basis-0 m:w-px"><p class="flex-1 shrink-0 basis-0 relative whitespace-pre-wrap w-px break-words type-body-1 text-black-token">003</p></div><div class="items-start flex flex-none flex-col gap-10 h-min justify-start overflow-clip relative w-full m:flex-1 m:shrink-0 m:basis-0 m:w-px"><div class="items-start flex flex-none gap-51.75 h-min justify-start overflow-clip relative w-full"><h2 class="flex-1 shrink-0 basis-0 relative whitespace-pre-wrap w-px break-words type-heading-4 text-black-token">Range</h2></div><div class="items-start flex flex-none flex-col gap-10 h-min justify-center max-w-177.5 overflow-clip relative w-full"><div class="flex flex-col justify-start shrink-0 flex-none relative whitespace-pre-wrap w-full break-words rich-text [&amp;_p]:type-body-2"><p>Most lasting palettes have one hero colour, one or two supporting colours and a set of neutrals. The hero carries recognition; the neutrals do the everyday work of backgrounds, text and layout. That balance keeps the brand recognisable without making every page loud.<br><br>We then build tints and shades for each colour so designers have enough range for charts, illustrations and interface states. Giving the team a clear, complete set means they rarely need to invent new colours, which is how palettes slowly drift and lose their character.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="items-center flex flex-none flex-col gap-2.5 h-min justify-center max-w-360 relative w-full m:flex-row"><div class="flex-none h-105 overflow-clip relative w-full rounded-[5px] m:flex-1 m:shrink-0 m:basis-0 m:h-130 m:w-px" style="opacity:0"><img alt="Friends laughing outdoors" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="rounded-[inherit] object-cover object-center" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="/images/blog/designing-for-motion-4.webp"/></div></div><div class="items-start flex flex-none flex-col gap-7.5 h-min justify-center max-w-360 overflow-clip relative w-full m:flex-row m:gap-47.5" style="opacity:0"><div class="items-center flex flex-none gap-2.5 h-min justify-start max-w-10 relative w-full m:flex-1 m:shrink-0 m:basis-0 m:w-px"><p class="flex-1 shrink-0 basis-0 relative whitespace-pre-wrap w-px break-words type-body-1 text-black-token">004</p></div><div class="items-start flex flex-none flex-col gap-10 h-min justify-start overflow-clip relative w-full m:flex-1 m:shrink-0 m:basis-0 m:w-px"><div class="items-start flex flex-none gap-51.75 h-min justify-start overflow-clip relative w-full"><h2 class="flex-1 shrink-0 basis-0 relative whitespace-pre-wrap w-px break-words type-heading-4 text-black-token">Longevity</h2></div><div class="items-start flex flex-none flex-col gap-10 h-min justify-center max-w-177.5 overflow-clip relative w-full"><div class="flex flex-col justify-start shrink-0 flex-none relative whitespace-pre-wrap w-full break-words rich-text [&amp;_p]:type-body-2"><p>Trends move quickly, and a palette chosen to look current today can feel dated in two years. We aim for colours that feel right for the brand first and fashionable second, so the identity can stay in use for a decade with only small refinements.<br><br>Finally, we document the palette with clear names, exact values for print and screen and simple examples of good and bad use. A well-explained palette is far more likely to be used correctly, and colour used consistently is what turns into lasting recognition.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="items-center bg-white-token flex flex-none flex-col gap-15 h-min justify-start relative w-full z-1 px-6 pt-6 pb-20 m:gap-20 m:pb-30 l:gap-17.5"><div class="flex-none max-w-360 relative w-full"><div class="items-center flex flex-col gap-3 h-min justify-center relative w-full m:hidden"><div class="flex-none h-px overflow-clip relative w-full" style="background-color:var(--color-black-a16)"></div><div class="flex flex-none items-center justify-between gap-4 h-min relative w-full"><p class="flex-none relative whitespace-pre type-body-3" style="color:var(--color-black-token)">More Articles</p><p class="relative min-w-0 truncate text-right type-body-3" style="color:var(--color-black-a60)">Keep reading</p></div></div><div clas